# Explainable AI-Based Chronic Kidney Disease Prediction and Diagnosis System

This document outlines the end-to-end plan for building a state-of-the-art web system for Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD) prediction. The system is designed to outperform standard research-level models by incorporating robust role-based user management (Patient & Doctor), prediction history tracking, interactive visualizations, and automated generation of clinical PDF reports with Explainable AI (SHAP, LIME, PDP) charts.

This project will be executed in a **structured, interactive learning format** tailored for a final-year B.Tech IT student. We will progress stage-by-stage, confirming understanding with concepts, questions, and practice tasks at each checkpoint before writing code.

---

## Interactive Learning Framework

To ensure maximum educational value and preparation for placements/viva, each of the **18 Stages** will follow this format:

1. **Theoretical Blueprint**:
   - Why we perform the task (clinical & technical motivation).
   - The underlying mathematical/algorithmic mechanisms.
   - Real-world relevance, best practices, and common developer mistakes.
   - Architectural/Design patterns to apply.
2. **Implementation & Walkthrough**:
   - Step-by-step coding with detailed line-by-line annotations.
   - Integration into the MVC/REST architecture.
3. **Assessment Checkpoint**:
   - Concept review and Viva-style questions.
   - A hands-on practice task for you to complete.
   - **Requirement**: We only proceed to the next stage after you review and approve/complete the assessment.

---

## Proposed System Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    %% Frontend (React Client)
    subgraph Client [React Frontend - Desktop & Responsive Mobile]
        UI[User Interface: Auth, dashboards, prediction panel]
        Viz[Interactive Plots: Plotly.js, SHAP/LIME charts]
        PDF[PDF Viewer & Downloader]
    end

    %% Backend (Django Rest Framework)
    subgraph Backend [Django Backend - REST APIs]
        Auth[Authentication & JWT Middleware]
        DRF[Django REST Framework ViewSets & Serializers]
        MLService[ML Inference & XAI Pipeline]
        Export[PDF & CSV Generation Service]
    end

    %% Data Store
    subgraph Storage [Database Layer]
        MySQL[(MySQL Database)]
        ModelsFile[(Serialized Models: .joblib)]
    end

    %% Flow Arrows
    UI -->|HTTPS Requests + JWT| DRF
    Auth -.-> DRF
    DRF -->|Query / Save Records| MySQL
    DRF -->|Features Payload| MLService
    MLService -->|Load Weights/Pipelines| ModelsFile
    MLService -->|Compute Predictions & SHAP/LIME values| DRF
    DRF -->|Format Response JSON + Visualizations| UI
    Export -->|Fetch clinical data & figures| DRF
    Export -->|Stream PDF| UI
```

---

## Database Schema Design (MySQL)

We will implement a relational schema supporting multi-tenant role-based access control, patient history tracking, and diagnostic logs.

```mermaid
erDiagram
    USER ||--o| DOCTOR : "has details"
    USER ||--o| PATIENT : "has details"
    DOCTOR ||--o| PREDICTION : "performs / reviews"
    PATIENT ||--o| PREDICTION : "receives"
    PREDICTION ||--|| EXPLANATION : "has XAI values"

    USER {
        int id PK
        string username
        string password
        string email
        string role "ADMIN | DOCTOR | PATIENT"
        datetime date_joined
    }

    DOCTOR {
        int id PK
        int user_id FK
        string license_number
        string specialization
        string phone
    }

    PATIENT {
        int id PK
        int user_id FK
        string medical_history_summary
        string phone
        date date_of_birth
    }

    PREDICTION {
        int id PK
        int patient_id FK
        int doctor_id FK "nullable (self-prediction)"
        datetime prediction_date
        float age
        float blood_pressure
        float specific_gravity
        float albumin
        float sugar
        string rbc "normal | abnormal"
        string pc "normal | abnormal"
        string pcc "present | notpresent"
        string ba "present | notpresent"
        float blood_glucose_random
        float blood_urea
        float serum_creatinine
        float sodium
        float potassium
        float hemoglobin
        float packed_cell_volume
        float white_blood_cell_count
        float red_blood_cell_count
        string hypertension "yes | no"
        string diabetes_mellitus "yes | no"
        string coronary_artery_disease "yes | no"
        string appetite "good | poor"
        string pedal_edema "yes | no"
        string anemia "yes | no"
        string predicted_class "ckd | notckd"
        float prediction_probability
        string risk_level "low | medium | high"
    }

    EXPLANATION {
        int id PK
        int prediction_id FK
        text shap_values_json "Feature contributions"
        text lime_explanations_json "Local surrogate details"
        blob shap_summary_plot "Serialized base64 image path"
    }
```

