## 18-Stage Execution Plan

Below is the curriculum we will follow chronologically.

| Stage | Name | Key Deliverables & Focus Areas |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **1** | **Project Planning** | UML Diagrams (Use Case, Sequence, Class, Activity), detailed analysis of the UCI CKD features. |
| **2** | **Environment Setup** | Directory structure, Python virtual environment, dependencies (`django`, `djangorestframework`, `xgboost`, `shap`, `lime`, etc.). |
| **3** | **Dataset Understanding** | Feature types (numerical vs. nominal), clinical significance of each lab parameter, identifying targets. |
| **4** | **Data Cleaning** | Handling carriage returns (e.g., `ckd\t`), stripping whitespaces, resolving missing value placeholders (e.g., `?`, `\t?`). |
| **5** | **Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)** | Univariate/bivariate analysis, distribution plots, correlation matrices, finding linear vs. non-linear relations. |
| **6** | **Preprocessing & Pipeline Design** | Imputation strategies (Median/Mode/KNN), encoding categorical variables, feature scaling. |
| **7** | **Feature Selection** | Pearson Correlation, Chi-Square testing, Random Forest feature importance selection. |
| **8** | **Model Training** | Training Decision Tree, Random Forest, KNN, SVM, XGBoost, LightGBM, ANN. |
| **9** | **Model Evaluation** | Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1, ROC-AUC, Confusion Matrix, Cross-Validation. |
| **10**| **Model Optimization** | Hyperparameter tuning using Grid Search and Random Search. |
| **11**| **Explainable AI (XAI)** | Calculating global and local interpretations via SHAP, LIME, PDP, and Permutation Importance. |
| **12**| **Model Serialization** | Packaging the preprocessing pipeline and optimal model weights via Joblib. |
| **13**| **REST API Development** | Serializers, authentication backends, predictions, history endpoints, role-based views. |
| **14**| **Django Backend Integration** | Core Django setup, models, database migrations, configuration parameters. |
| **15**| **React Frontend Development** | Building login panels, patient portal, doctor dashboard, interactive graphs, and dark mode. |
| **16**| **Clinical PDF Reports** | Generating patient diagnostic summaries with base64 embedded XAI charts. |
| **17**| **Dockerization** | writing Dockerfile and docker-compose files for local development and MySQL container orchestration. |
| **18**| **Cloud Deployment (AWS EC2)** | Security groups, Nginx reverse proxy configuration, Gunicorn daemon, application deployment. |

---

## Verification Plan

We will systematically verify each layer of the application:

### 1. Data & Model Verification
- Check data cleanliness checks (no special character classes left in nominal fields).
- Ensure preprocessing pipeline converts input dictionary formats (same format as API payloads) correctly without data leakage.
- Validate that serialized model loads and generates the exact same predictions as the trained Python model object.

### 2. Backend & API Verification
- Unit test REST endpoints using Django test clients:
  - Anonymous request to prediction endpoint $\rightarrow$ `401 Unauthorized`.
  - Patient request to write/read other patient's history $\rightarrow$ `403 Forbidden`.
  - Doctor requesting prediction history $\rightarrow$ returns patient details list.
- Profile latency of inference endpoints (target < 500ms, including SHAP/LIME computation).

### 3. Frontend & Visual Verification
- Browser testing of UI layouts (Responsive design, dark mode colors).
- Verify interactive Plotly charts rendering with appropriate tooltips.
- Validate generated PDF contents (all tables, risk levels, and SHAP diagrams are visible).

